    REFACTOR-0010: checkout depends on a PaymentProcessor, not on CoastPay
    
    checkout() can't be tested. It makes its own CoastPayTerminal, so a
    test can't choose what the charge returns. CoastPay approves or declines
    at random, and an approved charge is real money.
    
    Same fix as the coffee cart. payment.ts declares what checkout() needs,
    PaymentProcessor, with its contract. CoastPayTerminal implements it, so
    coastpay.ts now imports payment.ts instead of the other way round.
    main.ts is the one place that picks CoastPay, and passes it to
    checkout().

